od decorations have been preserved, giving a lot of charm to the museum rooms. Since its opening in 1950, the museum has been the setting for artistic events. \r\n\r\nSince 1980, the museum has been the headquarters of the NPO Centre Albert Marinus, which contains the collection (library, correspondence and writings) bequeathed by Albert Marinus (1886-1979), an internationally renowned sociologist and writer who dedicated his life to the study and promotion of intangible cultural heritage. The Centre Albert Marinus has a documentation centre and organises numerous cultural activities: exhibitions, publications, guided tours, on themes related to intangible cultural heritage. It has been recognised for its expertise in this field by UNESCO since 2016.\r\n\r\nAccessible to people with reduced mobility\r\n\r\nBus lines 27 and 29, stop Verheyleweghen\r\nMetro line 1, station Roodebeek\r\n\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"de":{"name":"Centre Albert Marinus (Museum Woluwe-Saint-Lambert)","address_street_name":"Rue de la Charrette","address_street_number":"40","address_street_box":null,"email":"musee.museum@woluwe1200.be","website":"http:\/\/www.albertmarinus.org","phone_contact":"+32 2 762 62 11","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1200","address_city":"Woluwe-Saint-Lambert","address_line1":"Rue de la Charrette, 40","address_line2":"1200 Woluwe-Saint-Lambert","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"Centre Albert Marinus (Mus\u00e9e de Woluwe-Saint-Lambert)","address_street_name":"Rue de la Charrette","address_street_number":"40","address_street_box":null,"email":"musee.museum@woluwe1200.be","website":"http:\/\/www.albertmarinus.org","phone_contact":"+32 2 762 62 11","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1200","address_city":"Woluwe-Saint-Lambert","address_line1":"Rue de la Charrette, 40","address_line2":"1200 Woluwe-Saint-Lambert","description_