tions":{"fr":"Visites Guid\u00e9es","nl":"Begeleide rondleidingen","en":"Guided tours","de":"Stadtf\u00fchrungen","it":"Visite guidate","sp":"Visitas guiadas","pt":null,"cn":null}},"others":{}},"languages":{"spoken":["fr"],"subtitles":[]},"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Art D\u00e9co et Modernisme \u00e0 Uccle : le quartier Longchamp","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"Aux portes de la ville, l\u2019ancien village d\u2019Uccle va devenir, dans l\u2019entre-deux-guerres, un lieu de r\u00e9sidence particuli\u00e8rement pris\u00e9 par les Bruxellois. Une expansion rapide conf\u00e8re \u00e0 certains de ses quartiers une grande homog\u00e9n\u00e9it\u00e9 de style, entre Art D\u00e9co et Modernisme. Cette visite guid\u00e9e illustre bien les diff\u00e9rentes tendances de l\u2019architecture de cette p\u00e9riode ainsi que la valeur d\u00e9corative de certaines de ses fa\u00e7ades.\r\n\r\nL\u2019\u00e9pisode 2 de cette visite entre Art D\u00e9co et Modernisme permet de parcourir un quartier moins connu et pourtant tr\u00e8s riche en patrimoine, le quartier Longchamp, qui compte sur son territoire quelques beaux exemples de maisons d\u2019architecte. \r\n\r\nLieu de d\u00e9part : Devant le Mus\u00e9e Van Buuren, Avenue L\u00e9o Errera 41","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.arau.org","email":"info@arau.org","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.559743"},"nl":{"name":"Art D\u00e9co et Modernisme \u00e0 Uccle : le quartier Longchamp","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.arau.org","email":"info@arau.org","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.559743"},"en":{"name":"Art D\u00e9co et Modernisme \u00e0 Uccle : le quartier Longchamp","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.arau.org","email":"info@arau.org","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.559743"},"de":{"name":"Art D\u00e9co et Modernisme \u00e0 Uccle : le quartier Longchamp","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.arau.org","email":"info@arau.org","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.559743"},"it":{"name":"Art D\u00e9co et Modernisme \u00e0 Uccle : le quartier Longchamp","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.arau.org","email":"info@arau.org","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.559743"},"sp":{"name":"Art D\u00e9co et Modernisme \u00e0 Uccle : le quartier Longchamp","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.arau.org","email":"info@arau.org","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.559743"},"pt":{"name":"Art D\u00e9co et Modernisme \u00e0 Uccle : le quartier Longchamp","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.arau.org","email":"info@arau.org","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.559743"},"cn":{"name":"Art D\u00e9co et Modernisme \u00e0 Uccle : le quartier Longchamp","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.arau.org","email":"info@arau.org","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.559743"}},"place":{"id":5171,"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e et Jardins Van Buuren","address_street_name":"Avenue L\u00e9o Errera","address_street_number":"41","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@museumvanbuuren.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museumvanbuuren.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 343 48 51","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1180","address_city":"Uccle","address_line1":"Avenue L\u00e9o Errera, 41","address_line2":"1180 Uccle","description_web":"Construite en 1928, la maison du banquier-m\u00e9c\u00e8ne David van Buuren pr\u00e9sente une architecture ext\u00e9rieure typique de l\u2019\u00c9cole d\u2019Amsterdam.\r\n\r\nL\u2019int\u00e9rieur, chef-d\u2019\u0153uvre de l\u2019Art D\u00e9co, offre un ensemble unique am\u00e9nag\u00e9 par des d\u00e9corateurs belges, fran\u00e7ais et n\u00e9erlandais de renom. Dans cette maison-mus\u00e9e, mobilier rare, tapis sign\u00e9s, vitraux, sculptures et tableaux de ma\u00eetres belges et internationaux, du XVe au XXe si\u00e8cle, sont rest\u00e9s \u00e0 leur place dans le cadre intime d\u2019une maison priv\u00e9e.\r\n\r\nLes jardins sont en eux-m\u00eames un chef d\u2019\u0153uvre de l\u2019art paysager. Fin des ann\u00e9es vingt, Jules Buyssens a con\u00e7u, dans l\u2019esprit Art D\u00e9co, le Jardin r\u00e9gulier, le Jardin pittoresque et la Grande roseraie. Dans les ann\u00e9es soixante, Ren\u00e9 Pech\u00e8re a cr\u00e9\u00e9 le Labyrinthe et le Jardin du c\u0153ur. Alice van Buuren a fait de ce parc un lieu de promenade, de m\u00e9ditation et de r\u00eave.\u200b","description_print":"27\/06\/2022\r\nLe mus\u00e9e et les jardins Van Buuren \u00e9taient la propri\u00e9t\u00e9 priv\u00e9e de David Van Buuren, banquier et m\u00e9c\u00e8ne n\u00e9erlandais, et son \u00e9pouse Alice Piette. Construite au XXe si\u00e8cle \u00e0 Uccle, cette villa Art d\u00e9co est un v\u00e9ritable \u00ab\u00a0conservatoire vivant\u00a0\u00bb o\u00f9 vous retrouvez autant de peintures, sculptures, vitraux ou encore mobilier rare. D\u00e9couvrez aussi des expositions temporaires.\r\n\r\nQuant aux jardins, ils sont un joyau de l\u2019architecture paysagiste des ann\u00e9es 1920. \u00c9galement de style Art d\u00e9co, ils ont \u00e9t\u00e9 con\u00e7us par Jules Buyssens et Ren\u00e9 Pech\u00e8re. Promenez-vous dans le Jardin pittoresque, baladez-vous dans le Jardin du coeur, faites un tour par la roseraie et perdez-vous dans le Labyrinthe. Dans ce vaste lieu de promenade, vous profiterez d\u2019un agr\u00e9able moment o\u00f9 m\u00e9ditation et r\u00eave sont les ma\u00eetres-mots.","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"Museum en tuinen van Buuren","address_street_name":"L\u00e9o Erreralaan","address_street_number":"41","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@museumvanbuuren.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museumvanbuuren.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 343 48 51","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1180","address_city":"Ukkel","address_line1":"L\u00e9o Erreralaan, 41","address_line2":"1180 Ukkel","description_web":"Het huis van bankier en mecenas David van Buuren werd in 1928 gebouwd. De buitenzijde kan als een typisch voorbeeld van de architectuur van de Amsterdamse School worden bestempeld.\r\n\r\nHet interieur is een meesterwerk van de art-decostijl. Het unieke geheel werd ingericht door befaamde Belgische, Franse en Nederlandse ontwerpers. In het museale huis heerst de intieme sfeer van een priv\u00e9woning, die wordt bepaald door de zeldzame meubelen, gesigneerde tapijten, glasramen, beeldhouwwerken en schilderijen van Belgische en internationale meesters. Stuk voor stuk bevinden zij zich nog altijd op hun oorspronkelijke plek.\r\n\r\nDe tuinen betekenen dan weer een hoogtepunt in de landschapskunst. De Gewone Tuin, de Pittoreske Tuin en de Grote Rozentuin werden eind jaren twintig door Jules Buyssens in art-decostijl ontworpen. In de jaren zestig legde Ren\u00e9 Pech\u00e8re het Labyrint en de Tuin van het Hart aan. Dankzij Alice van Buuren werd het park ingericht als een plek om te wandelen, te verpozen en te dromen.","description_print":"27\/06\/2022\r\nOoit was dit het priv\u00e9-bezit van de Nederlandse bankier en mecenas David Van Buuren en zijn vrouw Alice Piette. In deze art-decovilla in Ukkel vind je een schat aan schilderijen, beeldhouwwerken, glas-in-loodramen en zeldzaam meubilair. Er zijn ook tijdelijke tentoonstellingen.\r\n\r\nDe tuinen zijn een prachtig staaltje landschapsarchitectuur uit de jaren 1920. Jules Buyssens en Ren\u00e9 Pech\u00e8re ontwierpen ze in art-decostijl. Wandel zeker door de pittoreske tuin, de hartentuin en de rozentuin. Maar het klapstuk is het labyrint. Zorg ervoor dat je niet verdwaalt! Hier kan je volop genieten, mediteren of wegdromen.","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"Van Buuren Museum and Gardens","address_street_name":"Avenue L\u00e9o Errera","address_street_number":"41","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@museumvanbuuren.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museumvanbuuren.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 343 48 51","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1180","address_city":"Uccle","address_line1":"Avenue L\u00e9o Errera, 41","address_line2":"1180 Uccle","description_web":"Built in 1928, the house of banker and arts patron David van Buuren has an exterior typical of the Amsterdam School.\r\n\r\nThe interior, a tour de force of Art Deco, represents a unique ensemble brought together by renowned decorators from Belgium, France and the Netherlands. The rare furniture, carpets, stained glass, sculpture and paintings by Belgian and international masters from the 16th to the 20th century have remained in their original places, giving this museum the intimate character of a private home.\r\n\r\nThe gardens are a masterpiece of landscaping in themselves. At the end of the 1920s, Jules Buyssens conceived the Regular Garden, the Picturesque Garden and the Large Rose Garden in the spirit of Art Deco. In the 1960s, Ren\u00e9 Pech\u00e8re created the Labyrinth and the Heart Garden. Thanks to Alice van Buuren, this park is a splendid a place to stroll, reflect and dream.\u200b","description_print":"27\/06\/2022\r\nThe Van Buuren Museum and Gardens were the private property of David Van Buuren, a Dutch banker and patron of the arts, and his wife Alice Piette. Built in the 20th century in Uccle, this Art Deco villa is a real \"living conservatory\" where you can find paintings, sculptures, stained glass windows and rare furniture. It also hosts temporary exhibitions.\r\n\r\nAs for the gardens, they are landscape architecture jewels from the 1920s. Also in Art Deco style, they were designed by Jules Buyssens and Ren\u00e9 Pech\u00e8re. Stroll through the Picturesque Garden, the Heart Garden and the Rose Garden and lose yourself in the Labyrinth. In this vast walking area, you'll experience a delightful moment of meditation and daydreaming.","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"de":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e et Jardins Van Buuren","address_street_name":"Avenue L\u00e9o Errera","address_street_number":"41","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@museumvanbuuren.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museumvanbuuren.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 343 48 51","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1180","address_city":"Uccle","address_line1":"Avenue L\u00e9o Errera, 41","address_line2":"1180 Uccle","description_web":"Das Van Buuren Museum und die dazugeh\u00f6rigen G\u00e4rten waren einst Privatbesitz des niederl\u00e4ndischen Bankiers und M\u00e4zens David Van Buuren und seiner Frau Alice Piette. Die im 20. Jahrhundert in Uccle erbaute Art-d\u00e9co-Villa ist buchst\u00e4blich ein \u201elebendiges Schatzk\u00e4stchen\u201d, in dem unz\u00e4hlige Gem\u00e4lde, Skulpturen, Glasmalereien oder auch seltene M\u00f6bel verwahrt werden. Hinzu kommen sch\u00f6ne Wechselausstellungen.\r\n\r\nDie von Jules Buyssens und Ren\u00e9 Pech\u00e8re entworfenen Art-d\u00e9co-G\u00e4rten sind ein Kleinod der Landschaftsarchitektur der 1920er-Jahre. Flanieren Sie durch den malerischen Garten, schlendern Sie durch den Herzgarten, drehen Sie eine Runde durch den Rosengarten, verlaufen Sie sich im Labyrinth und geben Sie dabei sich voll und ganz der Meditation und Tr\u00e4umerei hin.","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e et Jardins Van Buuren","address_street_name":"Avenue L\u00e9o Errera","address_street_number":"41","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@museumvanbuuren.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museumvanbuuren.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 343 48 51","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1180","address_city":"Uccle","address_line1":"Avenue L\u00e9o Errera, 41","address_line2":"1180 Uccle","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"Museo y jardines de David y Alice Van Buuren","address_street_name":"Avenue L\u00e9o Errera","address_street_number":"41","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@museumvanbuuren.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museumvanbuuren.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 343 48 51","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1180","address_city":"Uccle","address_line1":"Avenue L\u00e9o Errera, 41","address_line2":"1180 Uccle","description_web":"Esta casa fue comprada en 1928 por en banquero y patr\u00f3n David Van Buuren, posee una magn\u00edfica arquitectura exterior t\u00edpica de la escuela de \u00c1msterdam. La decoraci\u00f3n de la parte interior est\u00e1 caracterizada por una decoraci\u00f3n art dec\u00f3 \u00fanica dise\u00f1ada en su totalidad por dise\u00f1adores belgas, franceses y neerlandeses. Los Van Buuren convirtieron su villa en una \"academia viviente\", donde muebles extravagantes, alfombras exc\u00e9ntricas, vidrieras, esculturas y obras maestras internacionales han permanecido en el lugar. El jard\u00edn, de un tama\u00f1o excepcional, ha sido restaurado. La casa se convirti\u00f3 en un museo en 1975 de acuerdo con el testamento de Alice Van Buuren.\r\n\r\nLa armon\u00eda era la principal preocupaci\u00f3n de David y David y Alice Van Buuren cuando dise\u00f1aron su casa, armon\u00eda en el estilo art dec\u00f3 del interior y armon\u00eda en los jardines que rodean la casa. En 1929, despu\u00e9s de empezar a cultivar el jard\u00edn, el banquero neerland\u00e9s, David Van Buuren(1886-1955) \u2014emparentado con la casa Orange-Nassau\u2014 y su mujer, Alice, construyeron su casa. Esta \u00e9poca fue una locura en Europa, ya que las \u00e9lites sociales s\u00f3lo buscaban el lujo sin l\u00edmites. Una aspiraci\u00f3n cumplida por los dise\u00f1adores y decoradores por su uso de materiales excepcionales(maderas ex\u00f3ticas, salientes, marfil, etc.). Soberbias colecciones de obras del s. XV hasta el s. XX, incluyendo una versi\u00f3n de \"Paisaje con la ca\u00edda de \u00cdcaro\" de Pieter Brueghel el Viejo. \r\n\r\nLos jardines cubren un \u00e1rea de 1'5 hect\u00e1reas incluyendo el \"Jard\u00edn del Coraz\u00f3n\" de R. Pech\u00e8re y el laberinto.","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e et Jardins Van Buuren","address_street_name":"Avenue L\u00e9o Errera","address_street_number":"41","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@museumvanbuuren.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museumvanbuuren.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 343 48 51","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1180","address_city":"Uccle","address_line1":"Avenue L\u00e9o Errera, 41","address_line2":"1180 Uccle","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"cn":{"name":"Mus\u00e9e et Jardins Van Buuren","address_street_name":"Avenue L\u00e9o Errera","address_street_number":"41","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@museumvanbuuren.be","website":"http:\/\/www.museumvanbuuren.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 343 48 51","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1180","address_city":"Uccle","address_line1":"Avenue L\u00e9o Errera, 41","address_line2":"1180 Uccle","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null}},"districts":[],"zones":{"list":[21],"translations":{"fr":["Sud"],"nl":["Zuid"],"en":["South"],"de":["S\u00fcden"],"it":["Sud"],"sp":["Sur"],"pt":[null],"cn":[null]}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":289,"location":{"lat":50.81005189,"lon":4.35382833},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2023-06-16T11:35:20+02:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:13:25+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"resto_ranking":0},"organizer":{"id":204134,"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Arau - Atelier de Recherche et d'Action Urbaines","address_street_name":"Rue du Midi","address_street_number":"165","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@arau.org","website":"http:\/\/www.arau.org","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 33 45","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du Midi, 165","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Comprendre Bruxelles pour mieux la d\u00e9fendre !\r\nL\u2019ARAU a \u00e9t\u00e9 fond\u00e9 en 1969, dans un contexte de \u00ab bruxellisation \u00bb et d\u2019exode des Bruxellois vers la p\u00e9riph\u00e9rie. L\u2019enjeu \u00e0 l\u2019\u00e9poque, toujours d\u2019actualit\u00e9 : d\u00e9fendre et promouvoir la ville habit\u00e9e et une qualit\u00e9 de vie pour tous les Bruxellois, ce qui s\u2019est traduit par d\u2019importantes contestations de projets de d\u00e9molition d\u2019une part et le d\u00e9veloppement de contre-projets d\u2019autre part, dans une optique de r\u00e9novation urbaine et d\u2019am\u00e9lioration du cadre de vie.\r\nL\u2019ARAU entend, par son action de sensibilisation et d\u2019information de la population, mettre \u00e0 disposition du public les outils n\u00e9cessaires pour suivre l\u2019\u00e9volution de la ville. Cette action se mat\u00e9rialise \u00e0 travers la publication d\u2019analyses et d\u2019\u00e9tudes, l\u2019organisation de colloques et d\u2019ateliers, des communiqu\u00e9s de presse, \u2026ainsi que de visites guid\u00e9es.\r\nCes visites, pionni\u00e8res en r\u00e9gion bruxelloise et organis\u00e9es depuis 1977, visent \u00e0 revaloriser la ville et ses atouts, \u00e0 d\u00e9velopper un regard critique sur ses transformations, ce qui passe par la sauvegarde et l\u2019entretien de son patrimoine.\r\nAu fil de toutes ces ann\u00e9es, l\u2019ARAU a d\u00e9velopp\u00e9 un riche catalogue de visites guid\u00e9es se d\u00e9clinant en diverses th\u00e9matiques : \u00ab Bruxelles incontournable \u00bb, \u00ab Architecture \u00bb, \u00ab Bruxelles en quartiers \u00bb, \u00ab La ville en transformation \u00bb, \u00ab Parcours d\u2019\u00e9t\u00e9 \u00bb, \u00ab Une maison bruxelloise \u00bb, \u00ab Bruxelles : ville de trams \u00bb, \u00ab Bruxelles sociale \u00bb, qu\u2019il est possible de d\u00e9couvrir lors de tours publics ou sous forme de visites priv\u00e9es, personnalisables.\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"Arau - Atelier de Recherche et d'Action Urbaines","address_street_name":"Zuidstraat","address_street_number":"165","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@arau.org","website":"http:\/\/www.arau.org","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 33 45","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussel","address_line1":"Zuidstraat, 165","address_line2":"1000 Brussel","description_web":"Brussel begrijpen om het beter te kunnen verdedigen!\r\nHet ARAU werd opgericht in 1969, in een context van \u201cBrusselisering\u201d en de uittocht van de Brusselaars naar de rand. De uitdaging van die tijd, die ook vandaag nog actueel is, bestond erin de bewoonde stad en de levenskwaliteit van alle Brusselaars te verdedigen en te bevorderen. Dat leidde tot grote protesten tegen afbraakprojecten enerzijds en de ontwikkeling van tegenprojecten anderzijds, met het oog op stadsvernieuwing en verbetering van de leefomgeving.\r\nHet ARAU wil met zijn bewustmakings- en voorlichtingsactie de bevolking de nodige instrumenten aanreiken om de evolutie van de stad te volgen. Deze actie neemt de vorm aan van de publicatie van analyses en studies, de organisatie van conferenties en workshops, perscommuniqu\u00e9s, enz. en rondleidingen.\r\nDeze rondleidingen, die baanbrekend zijn in het Brusselse Gewest en al sinds 1977 worden georganiseerd, hebben tot doel de stad en haar troeven tot hun recht te laten komen en een kritische kijk te ontwikkelen op haar transformaties, die ook het behoud en de instandhouding van haar erfgoed inhouden.\r\nIn de loop der jaren heeft het ARAU een rijke catalogus van rondleidingen over verschillende thema\u2019s samengesteld: \u201cOnmisbaar Brussel\u201d, \u201cArchitectuur\u201d, \u201cBrussel in wijken\u201d, \u201cDe stad in transformatie\u201d, \u201cZomerreis\u201d, \u201cEen Brussels huis\u201d, \u201cBrussel: stad van de trams\u201d, \u201cSociaal Brussel\u201d, die tijdens openbare rondleidingen of in de vorm van priv\u00e9rondleidingen op maat kunnen worden ontdekt.\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"Arau - Atelier de Recherche et d'Action Urbaines","address_street_name":"Rue du Midi","address_street_number":"165","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@arau.org","website":"http:\/\/www.arau.org","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 33 45","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussels","address_line1":"Rue du Midi, 165","address_line2":"1000 Brussels","description_web":"Understanding Brussels to better defend it!\r\nARAU was founded in 1969, in a context of \u2018Brusselsisation\u2019 and the exodus of Brussels residents to the periphery. The challenge at the time, which is still relevant today, was to defend and promote the inhabited city and a quality of life for all the inhabitants of Brussels. This led to major protests against demolition projects on the one hand and the development of counter-projects on the other, with a view to urban renewal and improving the living environment.\r\nThe ARAU intends, through its action to raise awareness and inform the population, to provide the public with the necessary tools to monitor the evolution of the city. This action takes the form of the publication of analyses and studies, the organisation of conferences and workshops, press releases, etc., as well as guided tours.\r\nThese tours, which are pioneering in the Brussels region and have been organised since 1977, aim to enhance the city and its assets, and to develop a critical view of its transformations, which includes the preservation and maintenance of its heritage.\r\nOver the years, the ARAU has developed a rich catalogue of guided tours on various themes: \u201cUnmissable Brussels\u201d, \u201cArchitecture\u201d, \u201cBrussels in Districts\u201d, \u201cThe City in Transformation\u201d, \u201cSummer Journey\u201d, \u201cA Brussels House\u201d, \u201cBrussels: City of Trams\u201d, \u201cSocial Brussels\u201d, which can be discovered during public tours or in the form of private, customised tours.\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"de":{"name":"Arau - Atelier de Recherche et d'Action Urbaines","address_street_name":"Rue du Midi","address_street_number":"165","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@arau.org","website":"http:\/\/www.arau.org","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 33 45","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du Midi, 165","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"Arau - Atelier de Recherche et d'Action Urbaines","address_street_name":"Rue du Midi","address_street_number":"165","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@arau.org","website":"http:\/\/www.arau.org","phone_contact":"+32 2 219 33 45","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du Midi, 165","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":nu