l,null,null]}},"facebook_link":null,"publication_state":"public","last_updated_at":"2023-07-08T03:05:57+02:00","published_at":"2023-06-01T17:05:29+02:00","backoffice_id":278528,"import_origin":null,"sub_type":"expo","show_in_agenda":true,"ranking":0.28543716208189},{"id":556593,"date_start":"2023-04-14","date_end":"2023-07-09","date_next":"2023-07-08","accept_article27":false,"accept_cultuurbon":false,"accept_paspartoe":false,"is_closed_on_public_holidays":false,"is_closed_on_school_holidays":false,"is_only_by_appointment":false,"is_permanent":false,"is_free":true,"is_online":false,"is_canceled":false,"is_soldout":false,"categories":{"main":{"id":23,"translations":{"fr":"Exposition","nl":"Tentoonstellingen","en":"Exhibition","de":"Ausstellung","it":"Esposizioni","sp":"Exhibici\u00f3n","pt":null,"cn":null}},"others":{"list":[36,43],"translations":{"fr":["Mus\u00e9es et art centers","Arts D\u00e9coratifs"],"nl":["Musea en kunstcentra","Decoratieve kunsten"],"en":["Museums and art centers","Decorative art"],"de":["Museen & Kunstzentren","Dekorative K\u00fcnste"],"it":["Musei e centri artistici","Arti decorative"],"sp":["Museos y centros de arte","Artes decorativas"],"pt":[null,null],"cn":[null,null]}}},"languages":{"spoken":["fr"],"subtitles":[]},"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Exposition UNIQUE(S)","shortdescr":"L\u2019exposition UNIQUE(S) met l\u2019accent sur les m\u00e9tiers d\u2019art appliqu\u00e9s \u00e0 la cr\u00e9ation contemporaine.","longdescr":"L\u2019exposition UNIQUE(S) met l\u2019accent sur les m\u00e9tiers d\u2019art appliqu\u00e9s \u00e0 la cr\u00e9ation contemporaine de mobilier et d\u2019objets usuels. Des mat\u00e9riaux les plus nobles aux mati\u00e8res novatrices encore peu usit\u00e9es, d\u00e9couvrez comment des cr\u00e9ateurs actuels perp\u00e9tuent le pr\u00e9cieux savoir-faire des artisans d\u2019art. Ces techniques, transmises de g\u00e9n\u00e9ration en g\u00e9n\u00e9ration, de mani\u00e8re orale sont une facette du patrimoine culturel immat\u00e9riel qu\u2019il importe de valoriser et de pr\u00e9server. \r\nL'exposition s'articule autour de plusieurs disciplines : \u00e9b\u00e9nisterie, luminaires, art de la table, verrerie, c\u00e9ramique, orf\u00e8vrerie, tapisserie, joaillerie, lunetterie ou encore gainerie. \r\nLes r\u00e9alisations de cinquante artistes belges et \u00e9trangers de r\u00e9putation internationale se d\u00e9ploient dans le cadre atypique et intime du Mus\u00e9e de Woluwe. \r\nL\u2019exposition est organis\u00e9e par le Centre Albert Marinus en collaboration avec le Centre d\u2019Innovation et de Design au Grand-Hornu et Atelier Jespers. \r\nConsultez le \u00ab Feuillet \u00bb \u00e9dit\u00e9 par le Centre Albert Marinus, enti\u00e8rement d\u00e9di\u00e9 \u00e0 cette exposition : https:\/\/www.albertmarinus.org\/Flip\/\r\n\r\nLe Mus\u00e9e de Woluwe est situ\u00e9 en bordure du parc Roodebeek, bel endroit de promenade disposant d\u2019un \u00e9tablissement o\u00f9 se restaurer.","performers":"Cinquante artistes belges et \u00e9trangers de r\u00e9putation internationale : Maarten Baas, Ben Storms, Goudji, Michele De Lucchi, Ado Chale, Xavier Lust, Daniel von Weinberger, Garouste & Bonetti, Pierre Bonnefille, Natalia Brilli, Domeau & P\u00e9r\u00e8s, Adeline Halot, Kaspar Hamacher, Gerard Kuijpers, Studio Krjst, J\u00f3lan van der Wiel, Tomas Libertiny, Ettore Sottsass\u2026","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.albertmarinus.org","email":"musee.museum@woluwe1200.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 762 62 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 762 62 11","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.556593"},"nl":{"name":"Tentoonstelling UNIQUE(S)","shortdescr":"De tentoonstelling UNIQUE(S) focust op de ambachten die worden toegepast bij de hedendaagse creatie.","longdescr":"De tentoonstelling UNIQUE(S) focust op de ambachten die worden toegepast bij de hedendaagse creatie van meubels en alledaagse voorwerpen. Van de edelste materialen tot innovatieve materialen die nog niet algemeen worden gebruikt, ontdek hoe de ontwerpers van vandaag het kostbare vakmanschap van de ambachten bestendigen. Deze technieken, die mondeling van generatie op generatie worden doorgegeven, vormen een facet van het immaterieel cultureel erfgoed dat moet worden bevorderd en bewaard. \r\nDe tentoonstelling richt zich op verschillende disciplines: houtbewerking, lichtontwerp, tafelgereiontwerp, glaswerk, aardewerk, edelsmeedkunst, tapijtwerk, juweelontwerp, brilontwerp en schedeontwerp. \r\nHet werk van vijftig Belgische en buitenlandse kunstenaars met internationale faam wordt tentoongesteld in het atypische en intieme kader van het Woluwe Museum. \r\nDe tentoonstelling wordt georganiseerd door het Albert Marinus Centrum in samenwerking met het Centrum voor Innovatie en Design van Grand-Hornu en het Atelier Jespers. \r\nLees de \u201cFeuillet\u201d uitgegeven door het Albert Marinus Centrum, volledig gewijd aan deze tentoonstelling: https:\/\/www.albertmarinus.org\/Flip\/ \r\n\r\nHet Woluwe Museum ligt aan de rand van het Roodebeekpark, een prachtige plek om te wandelen.","performers":"Vijftig Belgische en buitenlandse kunstenaars met internationale faam : Maarten Baas, Ben Storms, Goudji, Michele De Lucchi, Ado Chale, Xavier Lust, Daniel von Weinberger, Garouste & Bonetti, Pierre Bonnefille, Natalia Brilli, Domeau & P\u00e9r\u00e8s, Adeline Halot, Kaspar Hamacher, Gerard Kuijpers, Studio Krjst, J\u00f3lan van der Wiel, Tomas Libertiny, Ettore Sottsass\u2026","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.albertmarinus.org","email":"musee.museum@woluwe1200.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 762 62 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 762 62 11","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.556593"},"en":{"name":"Exhibition UNIQUE(S)","shortdescr":"The exhibition UNIQUE(S) focuses on the crafts applied to the contemporary creation.","longdescr":"The exhibition UNIQUE(S) focuses on the crafts applied to the contemporary creation of furniture and everyday objects. From the noblest materials to innovative materials that are not yet widely used, discover how current creators perpetuate the precious know-how of crafts. These techniques, passed on orally from generation to generation, are a facet of the intangible cultural heritage that is important to promote and preserve. \r\nThe exhibition is structured around several disciplines: cabinet making, lighting, tableware, glassware, ceramics, gold- and silversmithing, tapestry, jewellery, eyewear and sheathing. \r\nThe work of fifty internationally renowned Belgian and foreign artists is displayed in the atypical and intimate setting of the Woluwe Museum. \r\nThe exhibition is organised by the Albert Marinus Centre in collaboration with the Innovation and Design Centre of Grand-Hornu and the Atelier Jespers.\r\nRead the \u201cFeuillet\u201d published by the Albert Marinus Centre, entirely dedicated to this exhibition: https:\/\/www.albertmarinus.org\/Flip\/ \r\n\r\nThe Woluwe Museum is located on the edge of Roodebeek Park, a beautiful place to walk with an establishment offering snacks.","performers":"Fifty internationally renowned Belgian and foreign artists : Maarten Baas, Ben Storms, Goudji, Michele De Lucchi, Ado Chale, Xavier Lust, Daniel von Weinberger, Garouste & Bonetti, Pierre Bonnefille, Natalia Brilli, Domeau & P\u00e9r\u00e8s, Adeline Halot, Kaspar Hamacher, Gerard Kuuipers, Studio Krjst, J\u00f3lan van der Wiel, Tomas Libertiny, Ettore Sottsass\u2026","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.albertmarinus.org","email":"musee.museum@woluwe1200.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 762 62 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 762 62 11","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.556593"},"de":{"name":"Exposition UNIQUE(S\u00b0","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.albertmarinus.org","email":"musee.museum@woluwe1200.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 762 62 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 762 62 11","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.556593"},"it":{"name":"Exposition UNIQUE(S\u00b0","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.albertmarinus.org","email":"musee.museum@woluwe1200.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 762 62 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 762 62 11","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.556593"},"sp":{"name":"Exposition UNIQUE(S\u00b0","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.albertmarinus.org","email":"musee.museum@woluwe1200.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 762 62 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 762 62 11","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.556593"},"pt":{"name":"Exposition UNIQUE(S\u00b0","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.albertmarinus.org","email":"musee.museum@woluwe1200.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 762 62 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 762 62 11","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.556593"},"cn":{"name":"Exposition UNIQUE(S\u00b0","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.albertmarinus.org","email":"musee.museum@woluwe1200.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 762 62 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 762 62 11","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.556593"}},"place":{"id":243945,"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Centre Albert Marinus (Mus\u00e9e de Woluwe-Saint-Lambert)","address_street_name":"Rue de la Charrette","address_street_number":"40","address_street_box":null,"email":"musee.museum@woluwe1200.be","website":"http:\/\/www.albertmarinus.org","phone_contact":"+32 2 762 62 11","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1200","address_city":"Woluwe-Saint-Lambert","address_line1":"Rue de la Charrette, 40","address_line2":"1200 Woluwe-Saint-Lambert","description_web":"Le Mus\u00e9e de Woluwe Museum est le cadre des expositions organis\u00e9es par le Centre Albert Marinus et d\u2019autres activit\u00e9s culturelles ponctuelles (lectures, conf\u00e9rences, rencontres litt\u00e9raires,\u2026).\r\n\r\nImplant\u00e9 en bordure du parc de Roodebeek \u00e0 Woluwe-Saint-Lambert le Mus\u00e9e est install\u00e9 dans une maison particuli\u00e8re construite \u00e0 l\u2019initiative d\u2019Emile Devos \u00e0 la fin du 19e si\u00e8cle. De style atypique son architecture s\u2019inspire des maisons frisonnes (Nord de la Hollande). Une grande partie des d\u00e9cors d\u2019\u00e9poque ont \u00e9t\u00e9 conserv\u00e9s, donnant beaucoup de charme aux salles mus\u00e9ales. Depuis son ouverture en 1950, il est le cadre de manifestations artistiques. \r\n\r\nDepuis 1980, le mus\u00e9e est le si\u00e8ge, du Centre Albert Marinus asbl, constitu\u00e9 du fond (biblioth\u00e8que, courriers et \u00e9crits) l\u00e9gu\u00e9 par Albert Marinus (1886-1979), sociologue et \u00e9crivain de renomm\u00e9e internationale qui a d\u00e9di\u00e9 sa vie \u00e0 l\u2019\u00e9tude et \u00e0 la promotion du patrimoine culturel immat\u00e9riel. Le Centre Marinus dispose d\u2019un centre de documentation et organise de nombreuses activit\u00e9s culturelles : expositions, publications, visites guid\u00e9es, sur des th\u00e9matiques en lien avec le patrimoine culturel immat\u00e9riel. Il est reconnu pour son expertise en la mati\u00e8re aupr\u00e8s de l\u2019UNESCO depuis  2016.\r\n\r\nAccessible PMR\r\n\r\nBus ligne 27 et 29 arr\u00eat Verheyleweghen\r\nM\u00e9tro ligne 1 arr\u00eat Roodebeek\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"Albert Marinus Centrum  (Museum van Sint-Lambrechts-Woluwe)","address_street_name":"Karrestraat","address_street_number":"40","address_street_box":null,"email":"musee.museum@woluwe1200.be","website":"http:\/\/www.albertmarinus.org","phone_contact":"+32 2 762 62 11","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1200","address_city":"Sint-Lambrechts-Woluwe","address_line1":"Karrestraat, 40","address_line2":"1200 Sint-Lambrechts-Woluwe","description_web":"Het Mus\u00e9e de Woluwe Museum is het decor van door het Centre Albert Marinus georganiseerde tentoonstellingen en van andere specifieke culturele activiteiten (lezingen, conferenties, enz.).\r\n\r\nHet museum is gelegen aan de rand van het Roodebeekpark in Sint-Lambrechts-Woluwe en bevindt zich in een priv\u00e9woning die op initiatief van Emile Devos op het einde van de 19e eeuw werd gebouwd. De architectuur van dit atypische gebouw is ge\u00efnspireerd op de huizen in Friesland (Noord-Nederland). Een groot deel van de antieke decoraties is bewaard gebleven, wat de museumzalen veel charme geeft. Sinds zijn opening in 1950 is het museum het decor voor artistieke evenementen. \r\n\r\nSinds 1980 is het museum de zetel van de vzw Centre Albert Marinus. Dit centrum bestaat uit de collectie (bibliotheek, correspondentie en geschriften) die werd nagelaten door Albert Marinus (1886-1979), een internationaal vermaard socioloog en schrijver die zijn leven heeft gewijd aan de studie en bevordering van immaterieel cultureel erfgoed. Het Centre Albert Marinus beschikt over een documentatiecentrum en organiseert talrijke culturele activiteiten: tentoonstellingen, publicaties, rondleidingen, over thema\u2019s die verband houden met immaterieel cultureel erfgoed. Het is sinds 2016 door UNESCO erkend voor zijn expertise op dit gebied.\r\n\r\nToegankelijk voor mensen met beperkte mobiliteit.\r\n\r\nBuslijnen 27 en 29, halte Verheyleweghen\r\nMetrolijn 1, station Roodebeek\r\n\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"Albert Marinus Centre","address_street_name":"Rue de la Charrette","address_street_number":"40","address_street_box":null,"email":"musee.museum@woluwe1200.be","website":"http:\/\/www.albertmarinus.org","phone_contact":"+32 2 762 62 11","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1200","address_city":"Woluwe-Saint-Lambert","address_line1":"Rue de la Charrette, 40","address_line2":"1200 Woluwe-Saint-Lambert","description_web":"The Mus\u00e9e de Woluwe Museum is the setting for exhibitions organised by the Centre Albert Marinus and other occasional cultural activities (readings, conferences, etc.).\r\n\r\nLocated on the edge of the Roodebeek park in Woluwe-Saint-Lambert, the museum lies in a private house built at the initiative of Emile Devos at the end of the 19th century. The architecture of this atypical house is inspired by Frisian houses (North of Holland). A large part of the period decorations have been preserved, giving a lot of charm to the museum rooms. Since its opening in 1950, the museum has been the setting for artistic events. \r\n\r\nSince 1980, the museum has been the headquarters of the NPO Centre Albert Marinus, which contains the collection (library, correspondence and writings) bequeathed by Albert Marinus (1886-1979), an internationally renowned sociologist and writer who dedicated his life to the study and promotion of intangible cultural heritage. The Centre Albert Marinus has a documentation centre and organises numerous cultural activities: exhibitions, publications, guided tours, on themes related to intangible cultural heritage. It has been recognised for its expertise in this field by UNESCO since 2016.\r\n\r\nAccessible to people with reduced mobility\r\n\r\nBus lines 27 and 29, stop Verheyleweghen\r\nMetro line 1, station Roodebeek\r\n\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"de":{"name":"Centre Albert Marinus (Museum Woluwe-Saint-Lambert)","address_street_name":"Rue de la Charrette","address_street_number":"40","address_street_box":null,"email":"musee.museum@woluwe1200.be","website":"http:\/\/www.albertmarinus.org","phone_contact":"+32 2 762 62 11","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1200","address_city":"Woluwe-Saint-Lambert","address_line1":"Rue de la Charrette, 